    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added an `AUDIT` logger** (`src/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:75`) obtained via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` \u2014 matching the logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line** immediately after a successful save in `addOwner` (`:167`):\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n   Logging after `saveOwner` ensures the owner id is populated, and `customerCode`/`registrationDate` have already been assigned earlier in the method.\n\nThe emitted line (e.g. `owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`) contains the owner id, the customerCode, and the registrationDate, satisfying the test's `anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` assertion. The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1/1 tests).",
